@node straightel
@subsubsection straight.el

@lisp
(use-package eve
  :straight (:type git :host github :repo "behaghel/eve.el"
             :files (:defaults
                     ("scripts" "scripts/run-cli.sh")
                     ("cli/dist" "cli/dist/*.whl")
                     ("docs" "docs/eve.info" "docs/dir"))))
@end lisp

The explicit file groups are required: straight's defaults select Elisp files
but do not preserve these runtime and manual subdirectories.  The launcher must
remain at @samp{scripts/run-cli.sh}, the wheel under @samp{cli/dist/}, and the compiled
manual under @samp{docs/}.  Do not include a development @samp{cli/.venv} or unrelated
benchmark scripts.  After changing an existing recipe, run
@samp{M-x straight-rebuild-package RET eve RET} to refresh its file selection.

@node Manual
@subsubsection Manual

Clone the repository, add it to @samp{load-path}, and require it:

@lisp
(add-to-list 'load-path "/path/to/eve.el")
(require 'eve)
@end lisp

Opening any @samp{*.tjm.json} file then activates @samp{eve-mode} automatically.

@node Accessing the manual in Emacs
@subsection Accessing the manual in Emacs

Eve registers its bundled Info manual automatically when the package is loaded.
The recipe above includes the tracked, generated @samp{docs/eve.info} and @samp{docs/dir};
custom package recipes must retain those paths to provide the same integration.
Browse it with @samp{M-x eve-info} or @samp{C-h i m eve RET}.  The source manual is also
available as @samp{docs/eve.org} and online in the repository.  Contributors regenerate
the tracked Texinfo/Info artifacts after manual edits with
@samp{devenv -q shell -- docs}.

@node Quick Start
@section Quick Start

This walkthrough takes you from a raw recording to a rendered clip in five
steps.

@enumerate
@item
@strong{Transcribe a recording}

@example
M-x eve-transcribe RET
@end example

Select the directory containing your @samp{.mp4} files.  Eve starts
@samp{eve transcribe} in the background, keeps a visible @samp{Eve: transcribing…}
status in the mode line while it runs, and opens the manifest
automatically in eve-mode when it finishes.

@item
@strong{Read through the transcript}

Navigate with @samp{j} / @samp{k}.  The buffer shows each spoken segment as a block
of text.  Timestamps appear in the right margin.

@item
@strong{Delete unwanted content}

Place point on a word and press @samp{d} to delete it.  Press @samp{D} to delete the
whole segment.  Press @samp{f} on a word to tag it as a filler; press @samp{F} to
delete all tagged fillers at once.

@item
@strong{Compile a draft preview}

@example
C-c C-c
@end example

Eve validates the manifest, pre-renders changed segments in the background,
and produces a draft @samp{.mp4} in seconds.  Play it back with
@samp{C-u C-c SPC} or your usual player.

@item
@strong{Export for delivery}

@example
C-u C-c C-c
@end example

Compiles at full H.264 quality using the same segment cache.  Only
segments that haven't been cached yet need re-encoding.
@end enumerate

