@node Timestamp ruler
@section Timestamp ruler

@samp{eve-ruler-mode} (active by default) displays @samp{[hh:mm:ss]} markers in the
right margin.  Each marker is placed next to the segment that @emph{reaches} that
milestone in the rendered video — deleted content is excluded from the running
total.

The total rendered duration appears in the mode line.

@lisp
;; Change the milestone interval (default 30 seconds)
(setq eve-ruler-interval 60.0)
@end lisp

Toggle the ruler with @samp{C-c C-l} (@samp{eve-ruler-mode}).

@node Context panels
@section Context panels

@samp{C-c C-p} (@samp{eve-context-panels-open}) opens or refreshes the optional Eve
context UI when the @samp{context-panels} package is available.  It opens the side
panel plus the current-segment bottom editor, then focuses the bottom panel for
rapid review.  During the optional-first migration, Eve continues to work
without that package.

Opening the side panel disables the legacy right-margin @samp{eve-ruler-mode} while
the panel is active.  The side panel shows fixed rendered-timeline timestamp
landmarks using the same interval, anchored to the corresponding visible
transcript row when possible.  Internal segment ids are intentionally hidden.
Segments and markers with b-roll also get compact @samp{🎞} rows showing file
basename, duration, and configuration glyphs such as @samp{▣}
replace, @samp{⊕} overlay, @samp{◱} picture-in-picture, @samp{🎙} source audio, @samp{♪} b-roll
audio, @samp{🔇} mute, @samp{→} continue, @samp{▧} still, @samp{@{…@}} placeholders, and @samp{▭}
overlays.

The bottom panel is a current-segment cockpit.  It repeats the canonical timed
transcript words, shows segment timing/speaker/tags state, b-roll status, and
key-hinted action rows.  In the bottom panel, @samp{w} / @samp{b} move between visible
words, @samp{v} toggles a panel-local word selection, @samp{j} / @samp{n} and @samp{k} / @samp{p} move to
next/previous segments while keeping focus in the panel, @samp{q} returns focus to
the source buffer, and @samp{Q} closes the bottom panel.  Panel selection is visual
and does not mutate the source buffer's region.

@lisp
;; Enable local development integration outside eve.el itself.
(add-to-list 'load-path "~/ws/context-panels")
@end lisp

Set @samp{eve-context-panels-auto-open} to non-nil to open context panels
automatically when entering @samp{eve-mode}.

@node Hiding deleted segments
@section Hiding deleted segments

@samp{C-c C-h} (@samp{eve-hide-deleted-mode}) toggles visibility of deleted words and
segments.  When active (the default), deleted content is hidden and the
transcript reads as it will render.  When inactive, deleted content appears
with a strikethrough face.

@node Word-level display
@section Word-level display

@samp{C-c C-w} (@samp{eve-toggle-words}) shows or hides per-word timing annotations
under each segment.  Useful when inspecting or adjusting precise cut points.

